X:2
T:Pass the ball
T:Jamaican ring game
C:traditional (Jamaica)
O:Jamaica
R:ring game
S:Walter Jekyll (ed.), Jamaican Song and Story (London: David Nutt, 1907), Project Gutenberg #35410 (music as MusicXML), no. XCIV, p. 197
N:A Jamaican ring game in Jamaican Patois, as Jekyll printed it in 1907 (Allegro). The ring closes up tight, shoulder to shoulder; hands behind backs pass the ball round and round while the player in the middle tries to find it, and whoever is found holding it becomes the seeker. Everyone sings; "goin'" is one short syllable. Jekyll was an English collector in colonial Jamaica; credit the song to the Jamaican singers he heard. The mento band is ours, in the style of Jamaican country bands.
