X:3
T:Carry banana
T:Jamaican ring tune
C:traditional (Jamaica)
O:Jamaica
R:ring tune
S:Walter Jekyll (ed.), Jamaican Song and Story (London: David Nutt, 1907), Project Gutenberg #35410 (music as MusicXML), no. XCIII, p. 196
N:A ring game: the girl in the middle is supposed to carry a bunch of bananas on her head, and the singers comment and ask her questions ("Look! It is a nine-hand banana. No, a China banana. Did you find it? Did you steal it?"); the ring answers "carry banana", and "You find the banana?" is the signal to take a partner. "Tief" is Jamaican Patois for steal. Jekyll marks it Tempo di Valse. In the fourth line the word Jekyll printed for the variety, which can be heard as a mocking word for Chinese people, is sung "China", the name Jekyll gives the China banana (a stout low kind that withstands wind) in his own note.
Q:1/4=150
M:3/4
L:1/8
K:E
